{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T01:51:09Z","created_by_operation":"op_4cbdd047c3d84f04af7844b2bfb5955b","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_2e0f53730c6600e81363071e70dcfd9892eceae517417fa72b8b6f97c5ccbb39","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=limitations","setting":"gi-dellav/zerostack@efd142b3ac46 snapshot a1aca222966d5bd8","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_0a6a21896c12d1d99f5dec335a55231842d27ade0038773260478be88c442348","slc_4574740e9dcc575af365f4cfff6114a8798e67fe691fc34aa467283f863cfeba","slc_8f8d2ea808442662c7951fb346ce71a9668f9053967e2b8e7b31425309d1356c"],"source_ids":["src_3162a85b456b573aa7491e69cbdb0c41"],"text":"The README states Windows support is untested, and the loop and git-worktree features are explicitly marked experimental.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T01:51:09Z","updated_by_operation":"op_4cbdd047c3d84f04af7844b2bfb5955b"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T01:51:09Z","created_by_operation":"op_4cbdd047c3d84f04af7844b2bfb5955b","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_306860977918cce409e21758b1b7a17340a36c7a785fcaf9875ad3835445592b","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=memory-state","setting":"gi-dellav/zerostack@efd142b3ac46 snapshot a1aca222966d5bd8","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_6e6a1f6c7870508c12469dfbb22e1de57ca22f07b42b693ab5da62090ab32ebe","slc_7669224392a14d549345cc0747873056806d7d5f49c12198e24a3723a79fd6c1","slc_91683f713146ff0743a93c7e3850a3bb9511f75349e8e8917cce73d3dd804802","slc_aa5fdf3448e73f07eb8e5ba630adda570d870e02d342ac13f52d94a7a59d4c47"],"source_ids":["src_3162a85b456b573aa7491e69cbdb0c41"],"text":"The gated memory feature keeps plain-Markdown notes (global MEMORY.md plus per-project logs) injected into the system prompt each session; it is not in the default build.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T01:51:09Z","updated_by_operation":"op_4cbdd047c3d84f04af7844b2bfb5955b"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T01:51:09Z","created_by_operation":"op_4cbdd047c3d84f04af7844b2bfb5955b","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_37b0a4f25d1aeaebaec119c597b8ef81651b754990e4e8ca0b8d516104bd262b","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"gi-dellav/zerostack@efd142b3ac46 snapshot a1aca222966d5bd8","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_1e886dec07fae2628dfe8214dfe1770f358ea690d5c5492d5bc2449324a1d663","slc_7f2686d7aa269dfdfe36c7ee4ccb818a761a1ee4d3fbec7945990f239a6bb7ab","slc_98113d0816bb3e3ea8c531454e8e84407a68a406f81f160e498cbc504c3d18b0","slc_b2483e05b3c210ffc28a30a7eb04c5e007dfcb2003a6d3df95fe498a9d4585cd"],"source_ids":["src_3162a85b456b573aa7491e69cbdb0c41"],"text":"With the acp feature, zerostack acts as an ACP (JSON-RPC) agent server over stdio or TCP so editors like Zed can connect; ACP is not in the default build.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T01:51:09Z","updated_by_operation":"op_4cbdd047c3d84f04af7844b2bfb5955b"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T01:51:09Z","created_by_operation":"op_4cbdd047c3d84f04af7844b2bfb5955b","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_3f72a61abe0f3a003d982e22d44f8b8b41ad0b184cd8aabb9ac65a137376ea4f","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=tools-permissions","setting":"gi-dellav/zerostack@efd142b3ac46 snapshot a1aca222966d5bd8","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_4106e6599fab2b687372245e94701e0099d62ff8b21eadeb58e289d7cabef99c","slc_bb4307db9ddc5c450c8d602152b81b7a8347cc2087948425e105c1d73d2566e2","slc_c4792260cc629221f0ce20a3d2ed30155415e3bb347b97d6ab3d6c4621c2fcd9","slc_d7625c535900d5f6ddf1532f79097e4d01abc48743a3c7911a8084ffb2d7116e","slc_eb33e50f3aa3193b50b12d394a4deffd453a70fb406018395c5f8ef22770d8c2"],"source_ids":["src_3162a85b456b573aa7491e69cbdb0c41"],"text":"Optional --sandbox mode runs bash commands in bubblewrap (or zerobox on macOS), masks credential directories by default, and can require the backend via --sandbox-required; network stays on unless disabled.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T01:51:09Z","updated_by_operation":"op_4cbdd047c3d84f04af7844b2bfb5955b"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T01:51:09Z","created_by_operation":"op_4cbdd047c3d84f04af7844b2bfb5955b","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_4256c5f6432f8b6d742c10ed42857034047becc61bcd039200b6a0db939717d8","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=relevance","setting":"gi-dellav/zerostack@efd142b3ac46 snapshot a1aca222966d5bd8","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_3266845e2c13f81d9ae3424f50b516441fa96d609167e740e2e3d60fc915c6cd","slc_acadf97a9e38618010624fa3d61ce21dc8a312d1ef0a2a3ba41a1518cec376aa"],"source_ids":["src_3162a85b456b573aa7491e69cbdb0c41"],"text":"The project targets users wanting a lightweight terminal coding agent, citing ~30k LoC, a 26MB binary, and roughly 16MB average RAM versus much heavier JS-based agents.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T01:51:09Z","updated_by_operation":"op_4cbdd047c3d84f04af7844b2bfb5955b"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T01:51:09Z","created_by_operation":"op_4cbdd047c3d84f04af7844b2bfb5955b","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_554651672dc1cb2fea8824f44ec80296b586c644f10a545663483beb814a18fd","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=dependencies","setting":"gi-dellav/zerostack@efd142b3ac46 snapshot a1aca222966d5bd8","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_04ac27d6d0236ac2c9ab2ab6728c4132b7e683c1d94e0dc2a93097ff8cc3300f","slc_abedcb37446ee1cbac1ee4f46203ae4602b73a30d96bb867cbcc86458f044281"],"source_ids":["src_4686454d9b635fd19cf9705fc971d56a"],"text":"Core dependencies include rig 0.39, clap 4, crossterm 0.29, tokio, serde, pulldown-cmark, regex, reqwest, and mimalloc; optional features add rmcp (MCP) and agent-client-protocol (ACP).","updated_at":"2026-09-14T01:51:09Z","updated_by_operation":"op_4cbdd047c3d84f04af7844b2bfb5955b"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T01:51:09Z","created_by_operation":"op_4cbdd047c3d84f04af7844b2bfb5955b","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_70e6634cb4583ca020b9a5ffbe32929409d6431e540997ec6a1bc8bc483d079b","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=tools-permissions","setting":"gi-dellav/zerostack@efd142b3ac46 snapshot a1aca222966d5bd8","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_2489d97402abf0cf6de446d2e9fec8ddb842d10bf7a9ec16ab4b208ad8a155dd","slc_655428f5711bc78b84bb7fa10bd4e2960a045f1073b83e06b314ec067678f49d","slc_680c3be7f117aaf1012aaad4c6208a2a0e8a84370f66f9321f74f02f1fcb630d","slc_6e6a1f6c7870508c12469dfbb22e1de57ca22f07b42b693ab5da62090ab32ebe","slc_8fe3f02c749e769321d17b72487a77460eae86a815279de36c0db99070b48204","slc_be863119858a038c57485dbfe278aded4f3d4002f4dc3fc9b1f0420285b826ae"],"source_ids":["src_3162a85b456b573aa7491e69cbdb0c41"],"text":"There are five permission modes (restrictive, readonly, guarded, standard, yolo) with per-tool glob patterns, session allowlists, and doom-loop detection for repeated identical tool calls.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T01:51:09Z","updated_by_operation":"op_4cbdd047c3d84f04af7844b2bfb5955b"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T01:51:09Z","created_by_operation":"op_4cbdd047c3d84f04af7844b2bfb5955b","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_7ae34aa3c592b144e7522469a29ee2ccd1ec4888ae939185cf8bff32600a937c","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"gi-dellav/zerostack@efd142b3ac46 snapshot a1aca222966d5bd8","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_66cfd1fb63f44d5e4311f617b0e661b2f7c96f7edda3dae903c917781bcfdf2b","slc_979f9ba27409ad43c7d0ebe430964541fc2a68274d685804ee391d8efd005bef","slc_e879c4f2ac029e239eb08763d7dd2e164ed7bbd44b0ef793a94bf0799f2a8fc6"],"source_ids":["src_3162a85b456b573aa7491e69cbdb0c41"],"text":"A prompts system lets users switch built-in system prompts (code, plan, review, debug, ask, etc.) at runtime via /prompt, and custom prompts can be added as markdown files under the config prompts directory.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T01:51:09Z","updated_by_operation":"op_4cbdd047c3d84f04af7844b2bfb5955b"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T01:51:09Z","created_by_operation":"op_4cbdd047c3d84f04af7844b2bfb5955b","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_863568697c6018c7031fe8170fda8ad8cc16ec2284e1235912a0cd1487fce507","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=orchestration","setting":"gi-dellav/zerostack@efd142b3ac46 snapshot a1aca222966d5bd8","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_0a6a21896c12d1d99f5dec335a55231842d27ade0038773260478be88c442348","slc_1684e9b7e98b003b987fd314a99f9a457d3c125da1eeb18edceb636af9244818","slc_8ac40d154f4691506d573018de32baf3417ee84a606a65f345e0536b2a8ab8d0","slc_eebc61f463fb2123fb99127308575872b06df432fa689f3e8638e6ab36ff2e9f"],"source_ids":["src_3162a85b456b573aa7491e69cbdb0c41"],"text":"Git worktree integration offers /worktree, /wt-merge, and /wt-exit slash commands for a branch-per-task workflow, with optional auto-merge on exit; the feature is labeled experimental.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T01:51:09Z","updated_by_operation":"op_4cbdd047c3d84f04af7844b2bfb5955b"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T01:51:09Z","created_by_operation":"op_4cbdd047c3d84f04af7844b2bfb5955b","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_99ae4ebf9a0c929a178f2b2f2ec7bc5c3d90e96c7c94d0b7aedbee71df455c15","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=memory-state","setting":"gi-dellav/zerostack@efd142b3ac46 snapshot a1aca222966d5bd8","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_674af55889be76d190001923a32296ef98f5d2e96b5f2de8ab1bc5b751753bc7","slc_6e6a1f6c7870508c12469dfbb22e1de57ca22f07b42b693ab5da62090ab32ebe","slc_b1da8a7893f04adf396b9e762f1ea189e532b88fce3acc831a7605ad149e2f3c","slc_bf0067d8645c3022a7c0b3a0d7c620a53d2ea98de630651d67875c626f522217"],"source_ids":["src_3162a85b456b573aa7491e69cbdb0c41","src_4686454d9b635fd19cf9705fc971d56a"],"text":"Sessions are saved as JSON under $XDG_DATA_HOME/zerostack/sessions/ and can be resumed with -c, -r, or --session <id>; auto-compaction summarizes old messages near the context-window limit.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T01:51:09Z","updated_by_operation":"op_4cbdd047c3d84f04af7844b2bfb5955b"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T01:51:09Z","created_by_operation":"op_4cbdd047c3d84f04af7844b2bfb5955b","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_a2b75a0e028c8e9f9f14e85445c1c8bf8269f291b6c5b0bc5a9af8127dd4a72d","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=orchestration","setting":"gi-dellav/zerostack@efd142b3ac46 snapshot a1aca222966d5bd8","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_4574740e9dcc575af365f4cfff6114a8798e67fe691fc34aa467283f863cfeba","slc_50b7482b855609e6e59cf96582b656da3c13b64874f0f5056dd261128cba2057","slc_672e0bab96c5bec30d4d8b20aaf398ec26633e501762e840bfa88173758ca55f","slc_8001473596b50a04c75facb3b985e75be895b1d194fc98fa9e94e05df6ac41c9","slc_b8cbf1a98e55b94cfa845f65e6fc69dd36a084fa05d1d21b9c47a61d54e73427"],"source_ids":["src_3162a85b456b573aa7491e69cbdb0c41"],"text":"An iterative loop system (experimental) repeatedly works through a LOOP_PLAN.md plan with validation commands, usable via /loop in the TUI or headless flags like --loop-prompt and --loop-max.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T01:51:09Z","updated_by_operation":"op_4cbdd047c3d84f04af7844b2bfb5955b"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T01:51:09Z","created_by_operation":"op_4cbdd047c3d84f04af7844b2bfb5955b","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_a87e4289fb44c49fd9feb8892a2c8f7a5123517cecd82802b2d23e074e6dfee9","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=design-choices","setting":"gi-dellav/zerostack@efd142b3ac46 snapshot a1aca222966d5bd8","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_8e65510f9927b8af0049e47cb242b66bd7ee0fc5e192739099868510aae41c97","slc_b1da8a7893f04adf396b9e762f1ea189e532b88fce3acc831a7605ad149e2f3c"],"source_ids":["src_4686454d9b635fd19cf9705fc971d56a"],"text":"Provider abstraction uses type-erased enums (AnyClient/AnyModel/AnyAgent) instead of trait objects, and tokio runs single-threaded by default unless the multithread feature is enabled.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T01:51:09Z","updated_by_operation":"op_4cbdd047c3d84f04af7844b2bfb5955b"}
